{"version": 3, "term": {"cols": 110, "rows": 32}, "timestamp": 1794471536, "idle_time_limit": 2.0, "title": "Reliaburger 0.2.8: an agent debugs the platform"}
[0.049, "m", "The prompt"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2m# A planted Reliaburger bug: this relish was built from its own source with a past fix\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# (#1515) taken out. Claude Code gets the symptom, the Reliaburger plugin and a read-only\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m# token. Every line below is the real session as it ran. Idle time is cut to 2 s, and each slow step says how long it really took.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m» The prompt\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mTwo reports about `relish logs`, which we think come from one bug in\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[2mReliaburger itself, not in any app:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m1. The `quiet` app wrote a few lines when it started and has been silent\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m   since. Yet `relish logs quiet --since 5s` prints those startup lines,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m   which are older than five seconds. You can see this one on this cluster.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m2. On a bigger cluster, when the log store answers with no lines for an app\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m   and the node `relish` asks holds no local capture of that app (it runs on\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m   another node), `relish logs APP` fails with `404: no local capture for\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m   this workload` instead of printing nothing. This cluster has one node, so\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m   you can't reproduce it here.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mFind the function in Reliaburger's source that causes them, using\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m`relish agent source`, and say which file it's in. If you can, include a\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.59, "o", "\u001b[2m# Claude Code, model claude-opus-5-5\u001b[0m\r\n"]
