[0.059, "o", "\u001b[2m(refused or failed)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mExit code 2\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m{\"command\":\"report\",\"error\":{\"code\":\"usage\",\"endpoint\":null,\"hint\":\"relish agent --help lists the commands;…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.251, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[1m$\u001b[0m relish agent report --out ./report --patch fix.diff --site src/relish/client.rs:log_lines --title \"relish\r\n  logs: --since prints old capture lines, and an empty store answer surfaces a 404 from a node without the\r\n  capture\" --what-happened \"relish logs quiet --since 5s printed the quiet app's startup lines, which are much\r\n  older than 5s. On multi-node clusters, relish logs APP fails with '404: no local capture for this workload'\r\n  when the store returns no lines and the asked node doesn't run APP. Both come from BunClient::log_lines: its\r\n  skip-the-capture-fallback guard only checks start when a run instance is named, and it passes the capture\r\n  endpoint's 404 through even after the store has answered for the cluster.\" --expected \"--since with no\r\n  stored lines in the window prints nothing (the capture has no timestamps and can't honour a window). When\r\n  the store answered, a 404 from the local capture endpoint means the app isn't on this node, so the output is\r\n  empty and there is no"]
[0.0, "o", " error. If the store didn't answer, the 404 still surfaces.\" --not-tested \"Issue 2 was\r\n  not reproduced live (gym-1 has one node); the unit tests cover it. The gated suites (test-cluster,\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "  test-linux, test-slow, test-upgrade) did not run. The full portable suite had 10 failures that look\r\n  unrelated to this change (missing fuzz corpus and bench report files in the patch tree; MCP token tests\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "  picking up this session's token). patch try was still running when this report was drafted.\" --caught-by\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "  \"relish::client::tests::since_on_a_quiet_app_prints_nothing_from_the_old_capture and\r\n  a_node_without_the_capture_is_not_an_error_once_the_store_answered (all 51 relish::client tests pass with\r\n  the patch)\"\r\n"]
[0.051, "o", "\u001b[2m(refused or failed)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mExit code 2\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m{\"command\":\"report\",\"error\":{\"code\":\"usage\",\"endpoint\":null,\"hint\":\"relish agent --help lists the commands;…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.46, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m The value starts with `--`, so I'll pass it with `=`.\r\n"]
[3.788, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[1m$\u001b[0m relish agent report --out ./report --patch fix.diff --site src/relish/client.rs:log_lines --title \"relish\r\n  logs: --since prints old capture lines, and an empty store answer surfaces a 404 from a node without the\r\n  capture\" --what-happened \"relish logs quiet --since 5s printed the quiet app's startup lines, which are much\r\n  older than 5s. On multi-node clusters, relish logs APP fails with '404: no local capture for this workload'\r\n  when the store returns no lines and the asked node doesn't run APP. Both come from BunClient::log_lines: its\r\n  skip-the-capture-fallback guard only checks start when a run instance is named, and it passes the capture\r\n  endpoint's 404 through even after the store has answered for the cluster.\" --expected=\"A since window with\r\n  no stored lines in it prints nothing (the capture has no timestamps and can't honour a window). When the\r\n  store answered, a 404 from the local capture endpoint means the app isn't on this node, so the output is\r\n  empty and there is no "]
[0.0, "o", "error. If the store didn't answer, the 404 still surfaces.\" --not-tested \"Issue 2 was\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "  not reproduced live (gym-1 has one node); the unit tests cover it. The gated suites (test-cluster,\r\n  test-linux, test-slow, test-upgrade) did not run. The full portable suite had 10 failures that look\r\n  unrelated to this change (missing fuzz corpus and bench report files in the patch tree; MCP token tests\r\n  picking up this session's token). patch try was still running when this report was drafted.\" --caught-by\r\n  \"relish::client::tests::since_on_a_quiet_app_prints_nothing_from_the_old_capture and\r\n  a_node_without_the_capture_is_not_an_error_once_the_store_answered (all 51 relish::client tests pass with\r\n  the patch)\"\r\n"]
[0.057, "o", "\u001b[2m(refused or failed)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2mExit code 2\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m{\"command\":\"report\",\"error\":{\"code\":\"usage\",\"endpoint\":null,\"hint\":\"relish agent --help lists the commands;…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.141, "o", "\u001b[32m\u001b[1m$\u001b[0m relish agent report --out ./report --patch fix.diff --site src/relish/client.rs:log_lines --caught-by test\r\n  --title \"relish logs: --since prints old capture lines, and an empty store answer surfaces a 404 from a node\r\n  without the capture\" --what-happened \"relish logs quiet --since 5s printed the quiet app's startup lines,\r\n  which are much older than 5s. On multi-node clusters, relish logs APP fails with '404: no local capture for\r\n  this workload' when the store returns no lines and the asked node doesn't run APP. Both come from\r\n  BunClient::log_lines: its skip-the-capture-fallback guard only checks start when a run instance is named,\r\n  and it passes the capture endpoint's 404 through even after the store has answered for the cluster. The\r\n  existing tests since_on_a_quiet_app_prints_nothing_from_the_old_capture and\r\n  a_node_without_the_capture_is_not_an_error_once_the_store_answered catch both; all 51 relish::client tests\r\n  pass with the patch.\" --expected=\"A since window with no stor"]
[0.0, "o", "ed lines in it prints nothing (the capture has\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "  no timestamps and can't honour a window). When the store answered, a 404 from the local capture endpoint\r\n  means the app isn't on this node, so the output is empty and there is no error. If the store didn't answer,\r\n  the 404 still surfaces.\" --not-tested \"Issue 2 was not reproduced live (gym-1 has one node); the unit tests\r\n  cover it. The gated suites (test-cluster, test-linux, test-slow, test-upgrade) did not run. The full\r\n  portable suite had 10 failures that look unrelated to this change (missing fuzz corpus and bench report\r\n  files in the patch tree; MCP token tests picking up this session's token). patch try was still running when\r\n  this report was drafted.\"\r\n"]
[0.087, "o", "\u001b[2m{\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  \"command\": \"report\",\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  \"data\": {\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    \"dir\": \"./report\",\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    \"duplicate_of\": null,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    \"files\": [\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m      {\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m        \"bytes\": 7826,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m… 63 more lines\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.429, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m The report is drafted in `./report` and not posted. Checking on `patch try`:\r\n"]
[0.788, "o", "\u001b[2m(Read)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "\u001b[2m<system-reminder>Warning: the file exists but the contents are empty.</system-reminder>\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.211, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m I've finished every step except `patch try`: it's still booting the throwaway cluster, so the fix\r\n         hasn't been tried on a live cluster yet.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m **Where the bug is:** `BunClient::log_lines` in `src/relish/client.rs`, which `relish logs` uses.\r\n         When the log store returns no lines, it falls back to the node's own copy of the app's output (the\r\n         capture), which has no timestamps on its lines.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m 1. **Old lines with `--since`:** the code that should skip that fallback for a time window only looks\r\n         at `--since` when a run instance is also named. A plain `relish logs quiet --since 5s` falls back and\r\n         prints everything the capture holds. I reproduced this here: it printed `quiet`'s three startup\r\n         lines.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m 2. **The 404:** the fallback only reads the node you asked. When the store has already answered for\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         the whole cluster with nothing, a 404 from a node that doesn't run the app still comes back as an\r\n         error. I couldn't reproduce this one on this one-node cluster; only the unit tests cover it.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m **The fix:** skip the fallback whenever `--since` is set. Also record whether the store answered, and\r\n         if it did, turn a 404 from the fallback into empty output. If the store didn't answer, the 404 still\r\n         shows. The project's manual describes exactly this behaviour (issue #1515 in `docs/book/06-watching-\r\n         everything.md`).\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m **Results so far:**\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Build:** succeeded for both the local `relish` and the Linux binaries.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Tests on `relish::client`:** all 51 pass. This includes the two tests the bug breaks,\r\n         `since_on_a_quiet_app_prints_nothing_from_the_old_capture` and\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         `a_node_without_the_capture_is_not_an_error_once_the_store_answered`.\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Full suite:** 7850 passed and 10 failed. The failures look unrelated: fuzz corpus and benchmark\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         report files are missing from the patch copy, and some MCP token tests picked up this session's\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         token.\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Diff:** saved as `fix.diff`.\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Bug report:** drafted in `./report`, not posted. The posting command is `gh issue create --repo\r\n         reliaburger/reliaburger --title '…' --body-file ./report/issue.md`, to run once you've read it. Its\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         title is marked \"[unverified]\" because I gave no reproducer.\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m **About the JSON answer:** I had to submit it three times before the work finished, and every version\r\n         names the same app (`quiet`), fault kind (`relish_bug`), function and change. The patch in it was\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         written by hand from my edit before `patch diff` ran, so it differs a little from `fix.diff`: it has\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         one large hunk instead of three smaller ones. It hasn't been checked with `git apply`, so `fix.diff`\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         is the file to use. All three answers' summaries are also out of date: they say the client tests, the\r\n         diff and the report weren't finished.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m **Also worth knowing:** the source I read is from the `relish` binary's commit (2055dd2), while the\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         cluster's node runs e423d46. The bug is in the CLI's own code, so I don't expect that to change the\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         finding.\r\n"]
