[0.013, "o", "\u001b[2m1\t{\"command\":\"patch try\",\"data\":{\"api\":\"https://127.0.0.1:39017\",\"binaries\":[{\"bytes\":862052000,\"name\":\"bun…\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m2\t\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m3\t[exited with code 0]\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m4\t\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[9.145, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m I've now finished all the steps, including `patch try`. It booted a one-node throwaway cluster\r\n         (`patch-179fec14`) from the patched build, and it came up ready in 63 seconds. I didn't deploy an app\r\n         on it, so the fix still hasn't been run against a live `quiet`-style app.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m **The bug:** `log_lines` in `src/relish/client.rs` causes both reports. When the log store has no\r\n         lines, it falls back to the node's own copy of the app's output, which has no timestamps.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m 1. `--since` only blocks that fallback when a run instance is also named. So `relish logs quiet\r\n         --since 5s` printed `quiet`'s three old startup lines. I reproduced this on this cluster.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m 2. The fallback only reads the node you asked. When the store has already answered for the cluster, a\r\n         404 from a node that doesn't run the app still comes back as an error. This cluster has one node, so\r\n         I couldn't repro"]
[0.0, "o", "duce it live.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m **The fix:** always skip the fallback when `--since` is set. If the store answered, a 404 from the\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         fallback now means \"not on this node\" and prints nothing. If the store didn't answer, the 404 still\r\n         shows.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m **Checks:**\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Build:** succeeded.\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **`relish::client` tests:** all 51 pass, including the two tests this bug breaks,\r\n         `since_on_a_quiet_app_prints_nothing_from_the_old_capture` and\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         `a_node_without_the_capture_is_not_an_error_once_the_store_answered`.\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Full test suite:** 7850 passed and 10 failed. The failures look unrelated: fuzz and benchmark\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         files are missing from the patch copy, and some token tests picked up this session's token.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m **Files and answer:**\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Diff:** saved as `fix.diff`.\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **Bug report:** drafted in `./report`, not posted. It's marked \"[unverified]\" because I gave no\r\n         reproduction script. Once you've read it, you can post it with `gh issue create --repo\r\n         reliaburger/reliaburger --title '…' --body-file ./report/issue.md`.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m - **JSON answer:** my last one is the one to use; its `patch` is exactly `fix.diff`. Its summary\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         still says `patch try` hadn't finished.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m The source I read is the `relish` binary's commit (2055dd2), while the cluster's node runs e423d46.\r\n         The bug is in the CLI's own code, so I don't expect that to change the finding.\r\n\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m \r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1mclaude ▸\u001b[0m The throwaway cluster is still running. `relish agent patch destroy ./fix` removes it when you're\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "         done with it.\r\n"]
