[0.009, "o", "<!-- drafted by relish agent report; a human reads it and posts it -->\r\n\r\n### Fingerprint\r\n\r\n`rbfp-843dd60a2237` (error code none, finding none, site `src/relish/client.rs:log_lines`; seen on 0.2.8)\r\n\r\n### Version\r\n\r\nrelish 0.2.8, commit 2055dd28b5fde860e08bd6d1a37a9488894f56e6, source changed from that commit, aarch64-apple-darwin, formats protocol 58 / state 74\r\n\r\n### Fix status\r\n\r\nNot known: the agent didn't find a release with the fix.\r\n\r\n### What happened\r\n\r\nrelish logs quiet --since 5s printed the quiet app's startup lines, which are much older than 5s. On multi-node clusters, relish logs APP fails with '404: no local capture for this workload' when the store returns no lines and the asked node doesn't run APP. Both come from BunClient::log_lines: its skip-the-capture-fallback guard only checks start when a run instance is named, and it passes the capture endpoint's 404 through even after the store has answered for the cluster. The existing tests since_on_a_quiet_app_prints_nothing_from_the_old_capture "]
[0.0, "o", "and a_node_without_the_capture_is_not_an_error_once_the_store_answered catch both; all 51 relish::client tests pass with the patch.\r\n"]
[0.0, "o", "\r\nExpected: A since window with no stored lines in it prints nothing (the capture has no timestamps and can't honour a window). When the store answered, a 404 from the local capture endpoint means the app isn't on this node, so the output is empty and there is no error. If the store didn't answer, the 404 still surfaces.\r\n\r\n### Reproducer\r\n\r\nNone. This report is **unverified**: nobody has made it happen on purpose yet.\r\n\r\n### Evidence\r\n\r\n```shell\r\n{\r\n  \"evidence\": [],\r\n  \"fingerprint\": {\r\n"]
